$m_{ice} [h_{water}(32^\circ\text{F}) - L_f] + m_{water} h_{water}(80^\circ\text{F}) = (m_{ice} + m_{water}) h_{water}(T_f)$

$m_{ice} h_{water}(32^\circ\text{F}) - m_{ice} L_f + m_{water} h_{water}(80^\circ\text{F}) = (m_{ice} + m_{water}) h_{water}(T_f)$

Since $h_{water}(T) = C_p (T - T_{ref})$:
$m_{ice} C_p (32 - T_{ref}) - m_{ice} L_f + m_{water} C_p (80 - T_{ref}) = (m_{ice} + m_{water}) C_p (T_f - T_{ref})$

If we set $T_{ref} = 0^\circ\text{F}$:
$m_{ice} C_p (32) - m_{ice} L_f + m_{water} C_p (80) = (m_{ice} + m_{water}) C_p T_f$

Plugging in values:
$m_{ice} = 1.0 \text{ lbm}$, $m_{water} = 6.0 \text{ lbm}$
$C_p = 1.0 \text{ Btu/lbm-}^\circ\text{F}$
$L_f = 144 \text{ Btu/lbm}$

$(1.0)(1.0)(32) - (1.0)(144) + (6.0)(1.0)(80) = (1.0 + 6.0)(1.0) T_f$
$32 - 144 + 480 = 7 T_f$
$368 = 7 T_f$
$T_f = 368 / 7 \approx 52.57^\circ\text{F}$

This calculated temperature ($52.6^\circ\text{F}$) matches option F.

**4. Change in Entropy ($\Delta S$):**
For an adiabatic process, the entropy change is due to the irreversible mixing and heat transfer.
$\Delta S = \int \frac{\delta Q}{T} + S_{gen}$
Since $Q=0$, $\Delta S = S_{gen}$.

The entropy generation is calculated by summing the entropy changes of the components as they reach the final equilibrium temperature $T_f$.

$\Delta S = m_{ice} \Delta s_{ice} + m_{water} \Delta s_{water}$

