$$L = \lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{2}{\sqrt{\pi}} \sqrt{n} \int_0^1 (1-x^2)^n dx$$
This limit is related to the Laplace's method or the behavior of integrals of the form $\int_a^b f(x)^n dx$ as $n \to \infty$.

